  "result": "The concept `drv.road.opposed_directions` passed the gate with **OK** on the first run, using 1 of the 6 runs. It reports 3 witnesses and reads 1 atom.\n\n**Body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/road/opposed_directions.lean`):\n```lean\ndef dir (c : Arg) (k : String) : Term := .measure \"st_lane_direction\" [c, .lit k]\ndef dot : Term := .add (.mul (dir aC1 \"x\") (dir aC2 \"x\")) (.mul (dir aC1 \"y\") (dir aC2 \"y\"))\ndef body : Formula := .cmp dot .lt (.neg pOpposedCosine)\n```\nCore reads `st_lane_direction` normalised in the world frame. If either carrier has no direction, the comparison comes out unknown, which is what the contract asks for. The contract left no choice open, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/road/opposed_directions.lean`): the instance sets `opposed_cosine` to 9/10. In every scene c1 (region 100) is a lane designated east, with one stationary car on it.\n- **holds:** c2 (region 101) is the lane beside c1, designated west. The dot product is −1, below −0.9, so the result is compliant.\n- **fails:** c2 is a lane designated north that crosses c1. The dot product is 0, so the result is violated.\n- **blind:** c2 is a lane region with no lane record, so it has no direction, and the manifest masks `st.lane_direction`. The result is unknown.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
